Max says goodbye and we take a break.
Timo, Lena and I sit together on the bench.
Timo and Lena talk about a tournament.
"We played a tournament last week," Timo says.
Then Lena asks me about Berlin.
"Why did you choose Berlin?" she asks.
"And how did you find your job here?"
I laugh and begin my story.
"I saw the advertisement in October," I say.
"I wrote my application straight away."
"The company offered me the job very quickly."
"But then I waited a really long time."
"I filled out a lot of papers and forms."
"Then I booked an appointment at the embassy."
"All of that took a lot of time."
"Then in January I finally packed my suitcase."
"What did you pack?" Timo asks.
"Only clothes and my laptop," I answer.
"I only packed one big suitcase and a bag."
